Feature: Clock App Core Behaviour # features/app/clock_app.feature:1
  The Clock app shows the current local time (timezone-adjusted via the time manager) and the date
  where applicable. It updates once per second and updates the date when a new minute begins.
  The user can: (a) cycle between three display types (Digital, Analogue, Nixie simulation) by tapping,
  (b) temporarily toggle 12/24-hour format (future: persist this), and (c) briefly reveal the date.
  No alarm/chime functionality exists (removed). Persistence of format and display type is future work.
  @clock @time @tick
  Scenario: Time label updates every second  # features/app/clock_app.feature:12
    Given the system time is 12:00:05        # features/steps/clock_steps.py:37
    And the active app is "Clock"            # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    When one second elapses                  # features/steps/clock_steps.py:50
    Then the clock shows time "12:00:06"     # features/steps/clock_steps.py:76
    When one more second elapses             # features/steps/clock_steps.py:56
    Then the clock shows time "12:00:07"     # features/steps/clock_steps.py:76

  @clock @date @minute
  Scenario: Date label updates when minute changes               # features/app/clock_app.feature:24
    Given the detailed system time is Monday 2025-09-29 12:34:55 # features/steps/clock_steps.py:44
    And the active app is "Clock"                                # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    And the date label is currently hidden                       # features/steps/clock_steps.py:108
    When 10 seconds elapse                                       # features/steps/clock_steps.py:62
    And one more second elapses (minute rollover)                # features/steps/clock_steps.py:167
    Then the date label text becomes "Mon 29 Sep"                # features/steps/clock_steps.py:145

  @clock @format @encoder
  Scenario: Rotating encoder LEFT toggles format  # features/app/clock_app.feature:38
    Given the system time is 21:09:59             # features/steps/clock_steps.py:37
    And the active app is "Clock"                 # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    And the clock format is 24h                   # features/steps/clock_steps.py:80
    When I rotate LEFT on the encoder             # features/steps/clock_steps.py:92
    Then the clock shows time "09:09:59"          # features/steps/clock_steps.py:76

  @clock @date @popup
  Scenario: Encoder RIGHT shows date for 3 seconds then hides     # features/app/clock_app.feature:49
    Given the detailed system time is Tuesday 2025-09-30 08:15:10 # features/steps/clock_steps.py:44
    And the active app is "Clock"                                 # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    And the date label is hidden                                  # features/steps/clock_steps.py:108
    When I rotate RIGHT on the encoder                            # features/steps/clock_steps.py:125
    Then the date label is visible                                # features/steps/clock_steps.py:113
    When 2 seconds elapse                                         # features/steps/clock_steps.py:62
    Then the date label is still visible                          # features/steps/clock_steps.py:117
    When 1 more second elapses                                    # features/steps/clock_steps.py:56
    Then the date label is hidden again                           # features/steps/clock_steps.py:121

